Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:56:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 224/224] Tests: late admission with sink rejection through the
 engine-core loop

Late admission (0222) decides step N+1 when step N reaches the admission
layer, after taking the client requests that arrived meanwhile; sink
rejection (0221) holds each decoding request's last sampled token and
schedules it as draft zero of its next step. N's output is unprocessed when
N+1 is decided either way, so the held tokens and placeholders are the same;
what the later decision changes is which arrivals and aborts it sees.

tests/v1/engine/test_late_admission_sink.py runs the real
step_with_batch_queue around the real async scheduler and the sink tests'
scripted V2-runner worker, on the Say hi. collapse case:
- an arrival beside a held draft zero joins one step earlier with late
  admission, and both replies are identical with and without it (0 and 3
  drafter tokens, arrivals at three points);
- an abort that arrives while a token is held ends the request without
  emitting a token it never verified, its neighbour unchanged;
- a structured-output step sampled through the deferred path back-fills
  draft zero ahead of the drafts, and the grammar accepts committed tokens
  only, with late admission waiting on that deferred step.

tests/v1/engine/test_late_admission.py: the engine-core construction becomes
engine_core(scheduler, executor, late_admission, admit) for both files.

Upstream status: local; not proposed.
